This review replaces the conclusion in [the original incident](/kb/incidents/4471), not its historical evidence. The export is a snapshot from 4 October 2026; it does not establish current desk state or a deployed fix.

## What the executable views show

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Counts deduplicate report IDs and use tenant locale and booking form version. Browser locale and intake tags are intake guesses, not reliable causes. The second group was merged into a ticket for a different defect and needs its own engineering issue.

## Separate engineering work

### Shared parser reads month first

The parser accepts month-first dates even for day-first tenants. R-41200 reports 7 April becoming 4 July; R-41201 corrects the direction of its own report. Correct the shared parser using the tenant's expected format, and verify ambiguous and unambiguous dates across app and email entry paths. See [parser issue](https://github.com/AndreaBarghigiani/megadev-s01e03/issues/1).

### booking-v3 hint disagrees with the reader

booking-v3 prints MM/DD/YYYY while interpreting dates in the tenant's day-first order. R-41230 and R-41241 demonstrate the mismatch. Match the hint and reader to the same tenant format; test booking-v2 and booking-v3 across tenant locales. Fixing only the shared parser does not correct this misleading form. See [hint issue](https://github.com/AndreaBarghigiani/megadev-s01e03/issues/2).

### Five reports need investigation beyond those labels

R-41202 describes 12 May becoming 11 May; R-41209 describes June bookings a day off; R-41236 describes an invite arriving before booking; R-41344 describes different days in Lisbon and Toronto; R-41620 describes 6 October appearing as Monday. The table files these under parser by tenant. Their bodies do not prove a month/day swap, nor do they prove one shared alternative cause. Investigate date-only/timezone handling and send chronology, then split further if evidence warrants it. These reports overlap the parser group and must not be added again to the total. See [investigation issue](https://github.com/AndreaBarghigiani/megadev-s01e03/issues/3).

## Received is not merged

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The received series records when reports arrived; the merged series records desk actions. A merge spike is not an incident-onset spike. Neither series proves a fix, and reports continued arriving after the bulk merge. “Known” describes a desk label, not resolution.

## Engineering disposition observed after first submission

The challenge desk update reports: #4471 closed 05 October; parser fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`); hint won’t fix because booking-v3 form was retired. These are different dispositions. Parser issue #1 is closed as completed based on the desk report; hint issue #2 is closed as not planned because its form was retired. Neither is a locally verified production fix. The five anomalous bodies remain uncertain; investigation #3 is closed as not planned for this exercise, with no claim that those symptoms were repaired. Reopen with fresh reproductions if they persist.

## Change the triage decision

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and [triage guidance](/kb/triage/dedupe) were reviewed in 2024. Their subject-only rule can merge different causes and split one cause across different wording. Preserve that accepted record as history; [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-evidence-before-merge) supersedes it for this review. Match by evidence of cause, inspect body and tenant configuration, and leave uncertainty explicit. No product fix has been demonstrated here.

